#### Article 35

1. Special Protection as referred to in Article 34 paragraph (1) is carried out through:  
a. prevention so that Children do not become victims in emergency situations;  
b. recording the number of Children requiring Special Protection in emergency situations;  
c. mapping the basic and specific needs of Children requiring Special Protection in emergency situations;  
d. guarantee of security and safety of Children in Emergency Situations;  
e. recording of Children and their families for tracing and family reunification;  
f. priority emergency rescue, evacuation, and security measures;  
g. physical and psychological health recovery;  
h. provision of legal assistance, accompaniment, physical, psychological, and social rehabilitation of Children in Emergency Situations;  
i. care;  
j. improvement of facilities needed by Children in Emergency Situations;  
k. fulfillment of basic and special needs of Children consisting of food, clothing, housing, education, provision of health services, learning and recreation, security guarantees, and equal treatment;  
l. fulfillment of special needs for Children with Disabilities and Children experiencing psychosocial problems;  
m. exemption from education fees both conducted in formal and non-formal Educational Institutions during the emergency period; and  
n. provision of services for the fulfillment of Children's identity rights and important documents lost due to emergency situations; and/or provision of Social Reintegration services.  
2. Special Protection of Children in Emergency Situations as referred to in paragraph (1) must be received by Children in Emergency situations as soon as possible, the implementation of which is in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
3. Provision of services for the fulfillment of Children's identity rights and important documents lost due to emergency situations as referred to in paragraph (1) letter n is carried out by the Regency Government.

### Paragraph 2

Children in Conflict with the Law

#### Article 36

1. Special Protection for Children in Conflict with the Law as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter b is carried out through:  
a. humane treatment with attention to needs according to their age;  
b. separation from adults;  
c. provision of legal assistance and other assistance effectively;  
d. implementation of recreational activities;  
e. freedom from torture, punishment, or other treatment that is cruel, inhumane, and degrading to dignity and degree;  
f. avoidance of imposition of death penalty and/or life imprisonment;  
g. avoidance of arrest, detention or imprisonment, except as a last resort and for the shortest possible time;  
h. provision of trial before a Children's court that is objective, impartial, and in a closed hearing to the public.  i. avoidance of publication of their identity;  
j. provision of accompaniment by parents/guardians and persons trusted by the Child;  
k. provision of social advocacy;  
l. provision of private life;  
m. provision of accessibility, especially for Children with Disabilities;  
n. provision of education;  
o. provision of health services; and  
p. provision of other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
2. Special Protection for Children in Conflict with the Law as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through efforts of:  
a. prevention;  
b. administrative settlement of cases;  
c. rehabilitation; and  
d. social reintegration.

#### Article 37

1. Provision of legal assistance and other assistance effectively as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter c is provided in the form of:  
a. legal consultation, legal accompaniment, and defense in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;  
b. provision of language interpreters for Children in the legal process including sign language interpreters for Children with Disabilities;  
c. provision of information regarding the development of their case in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations; and  
d. provision of legal assistance and other assistance effectively in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
2. Implementation of recreational activities as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter d consists of daily free physical exercise activities in open spaces, daily entertainment activities, arts, or developing skills.  
3. Avoidance of arrest, detention, or imprisonment as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter g is carried out with attention to the child's age, type of crime committed, threat of crime committed, and criminal responsibility.  
4. Provision of justice before a Children's court that is objective, impartial, and in a closed hearing to the public as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter h is carried out by seeking a child-friendly court with standard facilities and infrastructure in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
5. Avoidance of publication of their identity as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter i is carried out by keeping confidential the name of the Child in Conflict with the Law, parents' names, address, face, and other matters that can reveal the identity of the Child in Conflict with the Law.  
6. Provision of accompaniment by parents/guardians and persons trusted by the Child as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter j is carried out to assist and provide strengthening to the Child so they are ready to follow the investigation, prosecution, and examination process in court hearings.  
7. Provision of social advocacy as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter k is intended to protect and defend Children in Conflict with the Law which is provided in the form of awareness of rights and obligations, defense, and fulfillment of rights.  
8. Provision of health services as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (1) letter o is carried out in promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative forms in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations in the health sector.

#### Article 38

1. Prevention efforts so that children do not come into conflict with the law as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letter a are carried out so that:  
a. Children do not become victims of criminal acts  
b. Children do not conflict with the Law; and  
c. Children do not commit criminal acts again.  
2. Prevention so that children do not come into conflict with the Law as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through:  
a. print media, electronic media, and online media;  
b. face-to-face in the form of counseling, discussions, lectures, campaigns; and  
c. outdoor media.  
3. Prevention efforts so that Children do not conflict with the law as referred to in paragraph 1 letter b are carried out through:  
a. dissemination;  
b. providing places or spaces for play, healthy recreation, and channeling Children's creativity;  
c. providing guidance on religious values and social values;  
d. conducting supervision of the environment that will have an impact on the occurrence of Children in conflict with the Law;  
e. increasing family resilience and welfare;  
f. providing coaching and skills training;  
g. providing places or spaces for play, healthy recreation, and channeling Children's creativity;  
h. providing religious guidance, social values, and good character;  
i. developing an environment that cares for Children in Conflict with the Law; and/or  
j. involving families in service, coaching, and guidance programs.

#### Article 39

Special protection for Children in Conflict with the Law in the form of administrative settlement of cases, rehabilitation, and social reintegration as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letters b through letter d is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 40

1. Prevention efforts so that children do not come into conflict with the law as referred to in Article 38 paragraph (1) are carried out by the Regency Government.  
2. Special protection for Children in Conflict with the Law in the form of rehabilitation as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letter c is carried out by the Regency Government in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

