#### Article 71

Supervision as referred to in Article 70 is carried out through:  
a. strengthening of families and the Community so that Children do not become victims of abduction, sale, and/or trafficking;  
b. monitoring in the surrounding environment so that Children do not become victims of abduction, sale, and/or trafficking; and  
c. reporting to authorized officials/agencies if abduction, sale, and/or trafficking occurs.

#### Article 72

Protection as referred to in Article 70 is carried out by providing a guarantee of security from threats that endanger the person of Child Victims of Abduction, Sale, and/or Trafficking in relation to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given.

#### Article 73

Prevention as referred to in Article 70 is carried out by:  
a. involving the Community in providing Special Protection for Children;  
b. increasing understanding related to abduction, sale, and/or trafficking of Children;  
c. establishing bilateral and multilateral cooperation, both national and international;  
d. increasing family resilience to prevent Children from abduction, sale, and/or trafficking; and  
e. increasing the responsibility of the Community, business sector, and mass media to protect Children from abduction, sale, and/or trafficking.

#### Article 74

Care and rehabilitation as referred to in Article 70 is carried out by:  
a. physical and psychological rehabilitation;  
b. medical services, such as reproductive tract infections and communicable diseases;  
c. mental health rehabilitation; and/or d. Social Rehabilitation.

#### Article 75

1. Supervision as referred to in Article 71 is carried out by the Regency Government in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
2. Protection as referred to in Article 72 is carried out by the Regency Government in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
3. Prevention as referred to in Article 73 is carried out by the Regency Government in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
4. Care and rehabilitation as referred to in Article 74 is carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

### Paragraph 9

Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence

#### Article 76

1. Special Protection for Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter i is carried out through efforts to:  
a. disseminate and socialize the provisions of laws and regulations that protect Children who are victims of violence; and  
b. monitor, report, and impose sanctions.  
2. Special Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) is provided in the form of:  
a. prevention;  
b. assistance;  
c. medical rehabilitation; and  
d. Social Rehabilitation.  
3. Handling of Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence as referred to in paragraph (2) is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 77

Dissemination and socialization as referred to in Article 76 paragraph (1) letter a is carried out through dissemination and mass media.

#### Article 78

1. Monitoring as referred to in Article 76 -37- paragraph (1) letter b is carried out by:  
a. observing and identifying the development of cases of physical and/or psychological violence against Children;  
b. anticipating problems arising from cases of physical and/or psychological violence against Children; and c. following up on cases of physical and/or psychological violence against Children.  
2. Reporting as referred to in Article 76 paragraph (1) letter b is carried out periodically or at any time according to needs.  
3. Imposition of sanctions as referred to in Article 76 paragraph (1) letter b is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 79

Implementation of Special Protection as referred to in Article 76 is also carried out in the education unit environment.

