2. Monitoring and reporting as referred to in Article 78 is carried out by the Regency Government.  
3. Implementation of Special Protection as referred to in Article 79 is carried out by:  
a. the Regency Government through Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the field of education;  
b. educators;  
c. education personnel;  
d. families; and/or  
e. the Community, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

### Paragraph 10

Child Victims of Sexual Crimes

#### Article 81

Special Protection for Child Victims of Sexual Crimes as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter j is carried out through:  
a. education about reproductive health, religious values, and moral values;  
b. Social Rehabilitation;  
c. psychosocial assistance during treatment until recovery; and  
d. provision of protection and assistance at every level of examination starting from investigation, prosecution, up to examination in court hearings.

#### Article 82

1. Education about reproductive health as referred to in Article 81 letter a is carried out so that Child Victims of Sexual Crimes:  
a. have understanding to be protected from the risk of sexual crimes; and  
b. know correct information about sexual education.  
2. Education about religious values and moral values as referred to in Article 81 letter a is carried out so that Child Victims of Sexual Crimes have strong faith and conviction to overcome their problems.

#### Article 83

1. Social Rehabilitation as referred to in Article 81 letter b is carried out in the form of:  
a. motivation and psychosocial diagnosis;  
b. care and nurturing;  
c. vocational training and entrepreneurship development;  
d. mental spiritual guidance;  
e. physical guidance;  
f. social guidance and psychosocial Counseling;  
g. accessibility services;  
h. social assistance and aid;  
i. resocialization guidance;  
j. follow-up guidance; and/or k. referral.  
2. In addition to the forms as referred to in paragraph (1), Social Rehabilitation is carried out in the form of:  
a. physical therapy;  
b. mental spiritual therapy;  
c. psychosocial therapy;  
d. therapy for livelihood;  
e. fulfillment of decent living;  
f. accessibility support; and/or  
g. other forms that support social functioning.

#### Article 84

Psychosocial assistance during treatment up to recovery as referred to in Article 81 letter c is carried out by:  
a. increasing self-confidence in Child Victims of Sexual Crimes;  
b. eliminating feelings of shame, doubt, and guilt in Child Victims of Sexual Crimes; and  
c. encouraging Child Victims of Sexual Crimes to have initiative.

#### Article 85

Provision of protection and assistance at every level of examination starting from investigation, prosecution, up to examination in court hearings as referred to in Article 81 letter d is carried out through:  
a. provision of information about the case process of Child Victims of Sexual Crimes and the right to obtain restitution;  
b. provision of assistance at the investigation, prosecution, and court examination levels; and  
c. provision of security and safety guarantees for Child Victims of Sexual Crimes.

#### Article 86

Implementation of prevention and handling of sexual crimes as referred to in Article 81 is also carried out in the education unit environment by educators, education personnel, and the Community in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
